# Normal user, v1 false positive — v2 correctly suppresses her.
# `alice` mistypes her password 5 times in 5 minutes at 10:00 from her
# usual IP (203.0.113.10) on her usual host (web01), then logs in.
# v1 fires R001 (brute force) + R002 (success after brute force, critical).
# v2 sees: known IP, known host, normal hour, no sudo abuse, no lateral
# movement, no staging — a 2-stage, low-rarity chain scoring below the
# incident threshold, so it is suppressed (auditable, not hidden).
# All IPs are RFC 5737 documentation ranges. Lab / sample data only.
